 Baal Mantra: Your AI-Powered Student Well-being Platform.

Baal Mantra is an intelligent early intervention system designed to detect, prevent, and manage student burnout. By combining real-time engagement analytics with a supportive AI companion ("Sathi"), it helps institutions proactively support students before they fall behind.

Key Features:
 Sathi AI Companion: A supportive, Gemini-powered chatbot for 24/7 emotional support and motivation.
 Smart Scheduling: One-click "Focus Block" scheduling directly to Google Calendar.
 Risk Analysis Dashboard: Real-time identification of "High Risk" students based on engagement patterns.
 Instant Intervention: Counselors can generate Google Meet links instantly for immediate support.
 Personalized Analytics: Detailed visualization of attendance, assignment completion, and engagement scores.


Tech Stack & Architecture:

• Frontend Framework: Next.js 16 & React 19
  - Where: Powers the entire client-side interface (`client/`), handling routing, layouts, and interactive components.
  - Why: Leverages the latest React 19 features and Next.js 16 optimizations for high performance and SEO. It provides a robust structure for building complex, interactive dashboards and ensures a seamless, responsive user experience.

• Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 & Lucide Icons
  - Where: Used for all UI components, layouts, and iconography.
  - Why: Tailwind (v4) offers a modern, utility-first approach for rapid, consistent styling with low bundle size. Lucide icons provide a clean, professional visual language critical for a mental health platform.

• Backend Runtime: Node.js & Express.js (v5)
  - Where: Serves as the API layer (`server/`), managing client requests, authentication, and orchestrating AI and data services.
  - Why: Event-driven non-blocking I/O is ideal for real-time applications. Express v5 allows for modern, robust routing and middleware handling, streamlining the development of RESTful endpoints.

• AI & Intelligence: Google Gemini Pro
  - Where: Drives the "Sathi" chatbot and analyzes student sentiment/risk patterns.
  - Why: Selected for its superior natural language reasoning and context handling. It enables "Sathi" to offer empathetic, context-aware support and actionable advice rather than generic responses.

• Data & Visualizations: Chart.js & In-Memory Store
  - Where: Admin/Student dashboards and backend data persistence.
  - Why: Chart.js renders complex engagement data into easy-to-understand visual trends. The In-Memory store (MVP) allows for ultra-fast prototyping and demonstration without the friction of database configuration, while remaining structured for easy migration to MongoDB/SQL.

• Integrations: Google Calendar & Meet
  - Where: Embedded in the scheduling and intervention modules.
  - Why: Directly connects digital insights to real-world actions, allowing students to block out focus time and counselors to initiate meetings instantly.

Google Technologies Powering the Solution:

1. Google Gemini 1.5 Pro (The Cognitive Core)
   - Usage: Powers "Sathi", the empathetic AI companion.
   - Why It Matters: Unlike standard rule-based chatbots, Gemini's advanced reasoning capabilities allow Sathi to understand emotional nuance, detect subtle signs of distress in student inputs, and offer personalized, context-aware motivation. It transforms the system from a passive tracker to an active, intelligent emotional support layer.

2. Google Calendar API (Action-Oriented Wellness)
   - Usage: Enables the "One-Click Focus Block" feature.
   - Why It Matters: Students facing burnout often struggle with executive dysfunction and scheduling. By deeply integrating with their personal Google Calendar, we reduce the cognitive load of planning. Sathi doesn't just suggest studying; it carves out protected time for it, turning advice into tangible action.

3. Google Meet API (Zero-Friction Intervention)
   - Usage: Instant counseling session generation.
   - Why It Matters: In mental health crises, every second of friction counts. We utilize the Google Meet API to generate secure, immediate video conferencing links the moment a counselor identifies a high-risk student. This eliminates the back-and-forth of scheduling, enabling immediate human connection when it's needed most.

